person "==Player\n<size:16>[Person]</size>\n\nPlays the game on a phone or desktop browser." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxQZXJzb24=>> as Player
rectangle "==MORE THAN ENOUGH\n<size:16>[Software System]</size>\n\nA mobile-first browser game: explore seeded layers, gather resources, grow living crystal and restore an underground teleporter. The first chapter focuses on manual gathering and the minimum win kit; machine activation unlocks later automation. Legacy worlds retain their earlier rules. Plain HTML/CSS/JavaScript with a bundled static client and development-only tooling." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxTb2Z0d2FyZSBTeXN0ZW0sR2FtZQ==>> as MORETHANENOUGH
rectangle "==Room Service\n<size:16>[Software System]</size>\n\nLets friends play one world together (server/): a Cloudflare Worker that makes rooms and a Durable Object per shared world that keeps the world and each player's progress, checks every message, and relays positions and edits between up to 100 players. The moderator can make a copy of a world to play as one of its players (server/src/copy.js), apart from the real one, download a whole world as a backup file and put a world that's gone back from one (server/src/backup.js), and has a page listing every world's players, sortable by progress (server/src/admin.js). It also keeps each player's own world for every device they link, by a secret sync key (server/src/vault.js, src/game/sync.js). See server/README.md for the rules and security limits." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxTb2Z0d2FyZSBTeXN0ZW0=>> as RoomService
rectangle "==Development Tooling\n<size:16>[Software System]</size>\n\nESLint static diagnostics with host-scoped globals, vendor exclusions and CI reports for correctness and complexity debt; test harnesses, deploy pipeline, benchmarks and art tools (3D-baked resource icons, rig and pickaxe reviews in art/). scripts/cultivation-playtest.mjs drives current-rule fresh worlds through controller commands and records the empty save and exact action/tick trace. A localhost-only playtestReplay host in src/game/main.js pauses the wall-clock adapter, replays the full journey through normal controller/UI handlers and validates state parity, caught faults and actual reload in test/browser.e2e.js. Legacy AUTO remains separate." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxTb2Z0d2FyZSBTeXN0ZW0sVG9vbGluZw==>> as DevelopmentTooling

